Procedure performed using the Olympus XP-190 endoscope. Patient positioned in left lateral decubitus with a standard bite block in place.

=== Page 4 === Upon entry into the oropharynx and passing the UES, the esophageal mucosa appeared normal. The Z-line was located at 38 cm from the incisors with no evidence of Barrett's esophagus.

The stomach was inspected with adequate insufflation. The fundus, body, and antrum were visualized with normal rugal folds and no erythema or erosions. The pylorus was patent.

The duodenum was examined up to the second portion and revealed normal villous architecture without evidence of inflammation or ulceration.

